## 5️⃣ Test Way 5: Lack of Token Invalidance and Replay Scenarios
This checks if a secret password recovery URL remains active indefinitely, failing to enforce expiration or single-use validation constraints.
## 📋 Step-by-Step Execution

   1. Trigger a password reset request. Retrieve the link from your email inbox.
   2. Use the link to successfully update your account password.
   3. Open Burp Repeater, re-construct the identical request string used to finalize the change password action, and hit Send a second time.
   4. Alternatively, wait 24–48 hours and send the token parameters again. [12] 

## 🔍 Response Verification Criteria

* Vulnerable Outcome ($1,500 Account Takeover): If the second request results in an HTTP 200 OK modification message or lets you alter credentials a second time, the token was not invalidated upon its initial use. It remains floating in memory, posing a continuous hijacking risk if intercepted from browser history logs.

